ificate design","localization proof"],"summary":"Define a boundary-augmented prefix LP that keeps late shadow thresholds visible when studying an early prefix. For example, the separated-block obstruction 0^N,c_0,0^L,c_1 has D_m=0 on the short prefix but a real shadow c_1 objective. Formalize an augmented value that captures this shadow and test whether repeated augmented defects force comparable-scale finite-prefix D_n.","title":"Boundary-Augmented Prefix LP","why_promising":"Iteration 14 showed ordinary shorter-prefix D_m misses late shadow conflicts; augmenting the prefix objective may be the right way to localize cross-scale incompatibility without making the false boundary-defect claim."},{"id":"idea_05","risks":"The two-level market structure may still admit a parity-like separator, so a proof attempt should actively search for moving-scale counterexamples.","suggested_lenses":["gluing theorem","counterexample search"],"summary":"Attack the restricted conjecture: for two positive levels ell<h in the formal left-limit deterministic known-path model, does D_n=o(n) imply existence of a fixed sublinear envelope and hence an anytime o(T)-regret policy? Use the single-drought and equal-low multi-low formulas as local lemmas, then either prove a dyadic localization theorem or construct a moving-scale repeated-drought separator.","title":"Two-Level D_n Gluing","why_promising":"This is the smallest nontrivial instance of the projective-consistency problem; solving or refuting it would clarify whether D_n is a real characterization or only a necessary certificate."},{"id":"idea_06","risks":"Computation may only reproduce known cases unless examples are designed to stress specific conjectures; numerical LP values also need proof before promotion.","suggested_lenses":["computational exploration","rational certificate extraction"],"summary":"Build an exact finite-prefix LP solver for small paths in the formal left-limit model, preferably outputting primal marginals and dua